    basic: "Keep track of the line! If the line already has Red, Yellow, and Blue, DO NOT play your Red card. If you only have Red, you are forced to take the penalty. Try to hold onto your 'Wild' cards for the 5th or 6th spot in the lineâ€”this is when you are most likely to complete a rainbow and take the points.",
    intermediate: "Cloud Management: If the line has 4 cards in it, and you have a Cloud, use it! While it seems bad to take the cards, taking 4 cards is better than waiting and being forced to take 10 cards later. This is called 'Tactical Collection'â€”clearing the board so your opponent doesn't get a huge victory pile on the next move.",
    advanced: "The 'Spectrum Trap': If you hold most of one color (e.g., you have 5 Greens), play your Green card early. This makes it very difficult for your opponents to complete a rainbow because you are hogging the green cards. They will be forced to play a duplicate or a cloud, allowing you to reset the line on your terms.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you have a hand of all the same color, you're in troubleâ€”try to cycle your cards as fast as possible.",
